00:42:40.260 --> 00:42:42.150
I mean duh.

00:42:42.150 --> 00:42:45.480
So that constraint
is non-convex.

00:42:45.480 --> 00:42:47.700
Everybody got that?

00:42:47.700 --> 00:42:49.170
Here's what's cool.

00:42:49.170 --> 00:42:54.050
If you do this, that's actually
a pretty good convex heuristic

00:42:54.050 --> 00:42:59.270
for getting a layout where
things are at least d apart.

00:42:59.270 --> 00:43:01.100
Everybody got this?

00:43:01.100 --> 00:43:03.470
And I could actually tune this.

00:43:03.470 --> 00:43:06.680
If these were squares,
for each edge,

00:43:06.680 --> 00:43:13.340
I could make d equal to
the radius of this one

00:43:13.340 --> 00:43:14.960
plus the radius of that one.

00:43:14.960 --> 00:43:17.450
And in that case,
it's a heuristic

00:43:17.450 --> 00:43:19.670
but I will tend to get
things that don't overlap.

00:43:23.710 --> 00:43:24.210
Make sense?

00:43:27.390 --> 00:43:29.520
So that's placement.

